{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-4-6","id":"msg_vrtx_01YSvDYB4xYXH6yeHAT5v74N","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Done. **Q10: Speculative decoding — speed up inference?** is written and committed.\n\n**What the note covers:**\n- **Root cause framing:** decode is memory-bandwidth-bound (~2 FLOPs/byte on A100), not compute-bound — one token per weight-load cycle\n- **Algorithm:** draft model generates K tokens autoregressively → target model verifies all K in one parallel forward pass → accept with `min(1, p_target/p_draft)`, rollback on rejection\n- **Lossless property:** the acceptance criterion preserves the exact target distribution — no quality degradation\n- **Real numbers:** vLLM `--speculative-model` with Llama 3 8B drafting 70B → ~2.8× throughput on HumanEval; α ≈ 0.75–0.85 for code, 0.30–0.50 for creative chat\n- **Variants:** Medusa (parallel heads on target, no separate draft model), n-gram drafting for boilerplate\n- **Pitfall coverage:** corrects the common misconception that it's \"approximate\" (it's lossless), and warns against assuming it always wins (α < 0.5 → may hurt)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":311,"cache_read_input_tokens":65051,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":311,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5c01508e-413f-4f60-b0db-9928a8cf62dd","uuid":"02a9b7ea-9af3-495f-9ced-6bf29504efd0"}
